Calc: the .xlsx export keeps formula cells outside of a matrix as packed runs of their row (16 bytes per cell).

The export created one XclExpFormulaCell record per formula cell (about 100 bytes with its slot in the row, plus a
compiled binary token array for a formula that is not shared) and held them all until the sheet was written. For
a 50 MB workbook of formulas (3.4 million formula cells) that was about 400 MB at the peak of saving, and a 200 MB
workbook of formulas ran out of 8 GB while saving as .xlsx. For .xlsx, a finished formula cell outside of a matrix
needs only its Calc cell, its cell format identifier and the "aca" (volatile) flag: SaveXml reads the formula text
and the cached result from the Calc cell when the sheet is written.

Each formula cell is still created as an XclExpFormulaCell, so cell formats, shared formulas, table operations and
the formula compiler see the same calls in the same order; the finished record is then replaced by a run entry,
and adjacent entries of a row merge through the existing TryMerge hook. The part of XclExpFormulaCell::SaveXml
after the matrix handling moves unchanged into a static helper, which both the record and the run call, so a
packed cell is written by the same code. Not used for the binary formats, for cells of a matrix or for the base
cell of a merged range.
New logic in sc/source/filter/inc/hstxlsxpackedformulas.hxx; hooks: the tail of XclExpFormulaCell::SaveXml split into a helper, 8 lines at the cell creation in xetable.cxx,
5 declarations in xetable.hxx. The environment variable HST_SC_XLSX_PACKED_FORMULAS_OFF keeps one record per
formula cell (used by the test to compare both paths).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0); the new file is LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary.
Test: CppunitTest_sc_subsequent_export_test6 testXlsxPackedFormulaCellsWriteTheSameSheet saves one document on both
paths (shared formula group, text, boolean and error results, a volatile function, bold formula cells, a matrix
formula, a formula in a merged base, a hidden row) and compares sheet1.xml, sharedStrings.xml, styles.xml and
workbook.xml; the sc export suites run on the new path; the large fixtures are saved on both paths and compared.
